{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C4v49yfsWdaqmH7NSf9Dka","type":"tool_result","content":"commit e7d61a75ad5f6c4db97e69bc4c57ffc02793377f\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Wed Oct 7 15:30:41 2026 -0600\n\n    build invocation 01 for item 349: the statement's acts and interventions are read from the item's commits\n    \n    Deletes the hard-coded `\"interventions\": []` and `\"acts\": []` attest.py\n    wrote into every statement and reads both from attavo/ledger.py's own\n    per-commit classification instead: acts carries each approve and merge\n    row as {act, sha, by, at}, interventions every amend, launch, and\n    transport row as {class, sha, by, at}. sha is now required in both\n    item shapes, and the predicate moves to attestation/v6; v3, v4 and v5\n    statements still read as sealed. Doctor's sixth proof recomputes both\n    lists for a v6 statement the same way it already does time and cost,\n    failing by name when they differ. item_ledger's own commit walk is\n    fixed to include a first spec commit that has no parent -- a fixture's\n    or a squash merge's root commit, which `^` cannot name and which `A..B`\n    would otherwise silently drop.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n attavo/attest.py                   | 15 ++++---\n attavo/doctor.py                   | 47 ++++++++++++++-----\n attavo/ledger.py                   | 76 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n schema/attestation.schema.json     | 18 ++++----\n tests/test_attest.py               |  6 +++\n tests/test_attest_interventions.py | 92 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n tests/test_attest_time.py          |  6 +--\n 7 files changed, 232 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)\n----\ncommit 1657577829a94994f88e3f7c92c776385f5faf05\nAuthor: attavo driver <driver@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Wed Oct 7 15:30:52 2026 -0600\n\n    attavo: build record for item 349 (build-01)\